-- title:
--   Coordinate exponent lists retain support size
-- statement:
--   Let $d\ge0$, let $q_i$ be nonzero natural numbers for $i<d$, and set $A=\prod_{i<d}\mathbb Z/q_i$. A primary coordinate for a prime $p$ is an index with $p\mid q_i$. For supports in $A$, write $Q_S$ for ordered-sum counts, $P_\chi(S)=\sum_{x\in S}\chi(x)$, and $\mathcal O_B(S)=(Q_S,(P_{\chi_i}(S))_i)$ for a character bank $B$. For each coordinate $i<d$ and finite support $S\subseteq A$, $$|E_i(S)|=|S|,$$ where $E_i(S)$ is the sorted coordinate exponent list. Repeated coordinate values retain multiplicity.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, Couret — Additive reconstruction: STROBO-4, singleton collisions and RECOH formal proof artifacts, https://zenodo.org/records/23980513; archive COURET_MATHEMATIQUES_20261105.zip, SHA-256 19a3b59aee930df74cab79c27b29e014843bd17179a26fef1261ed6b5a651ab7; file RECOH/lean/RecohCyclicPrimaryBank.lean, lines 73–78; source file SHA-256 430ca92ba25f4e25a54832978a347c9b3d98aef6735383f4f28b9a4fdaae66a1; theorem Couret.STROBO2TORS.recoh_cyclic_exponents_length

